len() – Returns the number of items in a tuple.
[index] – Accesses an item at a specific index.
[start:end] – Returns a slice of the tuple (end index not included).
list() – Converts a tuple into a list.
tuple() – Converts a list into a tuple.
del – Deletes the entire tuple.
+= – Adds/combines another tuple with the existing tuple.
+ – Joins two tuples together.
* – Repeats a tuple a specified number of times.

Tuple Creation:
    ("item",) – Creates a tuple with one item. The comma is required.
    ("item1", "item2") – Creates a tuple with multiple items.

Unpacking
    (a, b, c) = tuple – Assigns each tuple item to a variable.
    *variable – Assigns multiple remaining items to that variable during unpacking.

Looping
    for x in tuple: – Loops through each item in the tuple.
    range(len(tuple)) – Loops through the indexes of a tuple.
    while – Loops through a tuple while a condition is true.

Methods
    count() – Returns the number of times a specified value occurs in a tuple.
    index() – Searches for a specified value and returns its position.